<div class="y8">
<h1 id="title" class="y9">Your agents.<br>Within reach.</h1>
<div class="y10">
<p class="y11">Yorozu <span lang="ja">(よろず)</span> connects the AI agents on your Mac to your iPhone. Start a task, answer a permission request and read the result wherever you are.</p>
<div class="y12">
<a href="/beta" class="y13">Download for Mac</a>
<a href="/iphone" class="y14">Get for iPhone</a>
</div>
<p class="y15">Your Mac does the work. Your conversations stay with you.</p>
</div>
</div>

<figure class="app-window y17">
<img src="/assets/mac-demo-light.webp" alt="Yorozu on a Mac with a conversation about planning a Saturday outing, a searchable thread and a list of other conversations" width="820" height="540">
<figcaption>Yorozu on your Mac. Your iPhone stays in the conversation.</figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
</section>

<section id="next" aria-labelledby="next-title" class="y57">
<div class="y58">
<p class="y59">Mac and iPhone, together.</p>
<div class="y60">
<div class="y61">
<h2 id="next-title" class="y62">Your Mac does the work.</h2>
<p class="y63">Reach it from your phone. Keep your host Mac awake and online.</p>
</div>
<div class="y64">
<div class="y65">
<h3 class="y66">Host on your own Mac</h3>
<p class="y67">Yorozu runs your agents on the machine you already use. Your files and tools stay on that Mac.</p>
</div>
<div class="y65">
<h3 class="y66">Connect with OpenClaw</h3>
<p class="y67">Add Yorozu as a chat channel for OpenClaw, using the providers, models and tools you have configured there.</p>
</div>
<div class="y65">
<h3 class="y66">Pick up a conversation</h3>
<p class="y67">Start on your Mac and continue on your phone. Paired devices reach the same threads.</p>
</div>
<div class="y65">
<h3 class="y66">Make the decision</h3>
<p class="y67">When an agent asks for permission, review the action on your iPhone. Allow it, refuse it or discuss it first.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section id="today" aria-labelledby="today-title" class="y68">
<div class="y69">
<div class="y70">
<div class="y71">
<div class="y61">
<h2 id="today-title" class="y72">Keep the conversation going.</h2>
<p class="y73">Your Mac hosts the agents through OpenClaw. Your iPhone reaches them: start a task on the train, answer a permission request from the lock screen, read the result at your desk.</p>
</div>
<dl class="y74">
<div class="y54">
<dt class="y75">Approve from your phone</dt>
<dd class="y76">When an agent wants to run a command, send a message or spend money, the question arrives as a card you can allow, refuse or discuss first.</dd>
</div>
<div class="y54">
<dt class="y75">Threads on every device</dt>
<dd class="y76">Threads sync between the Mac and every paired device, iPhone Duo included. Pair several Macs and see them in one list.</dd>
</div>
<div class="y54">
<dt class="y75">Search and share</dt>
<dd class="y76">Search the full history on your Mac, and send a link, some text or a photo into a thread from the share sheet.</dd>
</div>
<div class="y54">
<dt class="y75">Encrypted end to end</dt>
<dd class="y76">Messages are encrypted between your iPhone and your Mac. The relay in the middle sees size and timing. No Yorozu account is needed.</dd>
</div>
</dl>
</div>

<figure class="current-phone"><img src="/assets/iphone-approval.webp" alt="Yorozu iPhone approval screen with Allow once, For this task, Don’t allow and Discuss first" width="804" height="1748" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Approve an action from your iPhone.</figcaption></figure>
</div>

