<section id="setup-with-an-agent" aria-labelledby="setup-title" class="y57">
<div class="y83">

<div class="y84">
<div class="y85">
<h2 id="setup-title" class="y86">Set it up with one prompt.</h2>
<p class="y87">Paste it into a coding agent on your Mac. It checks what you already have, then walks you through both apps, permissions, OpenClaw with its Yorozu channel, and pairing your iPhone. It asks before every change.</p>
</div>
<div class="y88">
<div class="y89">
<p id="agent-prompt" class="y90">Read https://raw.githubusercontent.com/izyuumi/yorozu/main/Start.md and follow it to set up Yorozu on my devices. Ask me before configuring anything.</p>
<button type="button" data-copy="agent-prompt" hidden class="y91">Copy</button>
</div>
<p class="y92"><span id="agent-prompt-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></span>The guide is <a href="https://github.com/izyuumi/yorozu/blob/main/Start.md" class="y16">Start.md</a> in the repository. Read <a href="#before-you-install" class="y16">Before you install</a> first.</p>
</div>
</div>

<div id="pair" class="y71">
<div class="y93">
<h2 class="y86">Or pair by hand.</h2>
<p class="y94">Keep your host Mac awake and online to reach it from your phone.</p>
</div>
<ol class="y95">
<li class="y65">
<span aria-hidden="true" class="y96">1</span>
<h3 class="y97">Set up your host Mac</h3>
<p class="y87">Open Yorozu from the menu bar, choose “Host Yorozu on this Mac” and grant the permissions you want. Then add Yorozu to OpenClaw as a chat channel with <a href="https://github.com/izyuumi/yorozu#install" class="y16">four commands</a>.</p>
</li>
<li class="y65">
<span aria-hidden="true" class="y96">2</span>
<h3 class="y97">Scan one code</h3>
<p class="y87">In Mac Settings, under Devices, choose “Pair Another Device”. Open Yorozu on your iPhone and scan the code.</p>
</li>
<li class="y65">
<span aria-hidden="true" class="y96">3</span>
<h3 class="y97">Talk from anywhere</h3>
<p class="y87">Every thread lives on the Mac. Your phone, and any other Mac, just reaches it.</p>
</li>
</ol>
</div>

<div id="before-you-install" class="y98">
<h2 class="y99">Before you install</h2>
<div class="y100">
<p class="y101"><strong>Using Yorozu could get your Claude or ChatGPT/Codex account suspended or banned.</strong> Yorozu drives Claude Code and Codex on your Mac with the account you signed in with. Anthropic and OpenAI decide what use of their subscriptions is allowed, change those rules without notice, and have suspended accounts used with third-party agent tools. If you want the lowest risk, use an API key rather than a subscription login.</p>
<p class="y101">AI agents take real actions on your Mac: they run commands, edit and delete files, and can send messages. Review what you approve. See the <a href="/terms/" class="y16">Terms of Use</a>.</p>
</div>
